WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:04.570
Lamp for reps. Part five: funders and offers.

2
00:00:05.050 --> 00:00:11.420
Funders lists who Lamp sends files to, and what each one takes. Admins keep it up to date.

3
00:00:11.710 --> 00:00:18.380
Each funder shows its range, minimum deposits, time in business, and how many positions it allows.

4
00:00:18.930 --> 00:00:23.080
On a file, Send to funders shows which funders match it.

5
00:00:23.380 --> 00:00:29.250
A file needs two things before it can go out: the signed application, and three bank statements.

6
00:00:29.830 --> 00:00:38.000
Once both are in, tick the funders, preview the email, and send. Each funder gets its own email, from the partners mailbox.

7
00:00:38.620 --> 00:00:42.190
Funders and offers tracks every send and every offer.

8
00:00:42.590 --> 00:00:48.520
Sent to lists each funder and where they stand: sent, offer in, or declined.

9
00:00:49.020 --> 00:00:58.110
When a funder sends an offer, click Add an offer, and type it in: the amount, the total payback, the fees, and the number of payments.

10
00:01:01.870 --> 00:01:04.840
Lamp does the math. Here's how to read an offer.

11
00:01:05.250 --> 00:01:12.080
The amount is what the funder advances. Payback is what the merchant pays back in total.

12
00:01:12.490 --> 00:01:18.960
Factor is payback divided by the amount. 1.29 means they pay back a dollar twenty-nine for every dollar.

13
00:01:19.380 --> 00:01:23.890
Payments shows how many, how often, and how much each one is.

14
00:01:24.330 --> 00:01:29.560
Fees come out first. What lands in the account is the amount minus fees.

15
00:01:30.130 --> 00:01:36.500
Total cost is everything above what lands in the account. Walk the merchant through all of it.

16
00:01:36.800 --> 00:01:41.250
Saved offers stay hidden from the merchant until you click Show to merchant.

17
00:01:41.650 --> 00:01:48.720
The merchant accepts in their account, or you mark it Merchant accepted. Any other offers on the file are declined.

18
00:01:49.230 --> 00:01:55.200
Never call it a loan. It's an advance on future sales. Say advance or funding.

19
00:01:55.640 --> 00:01:57.090
Next: your numbers.
